Z||000000||nivlek68||07-23-2000||03:10 PM||||i just msde a long trip, and the rear tires are worn on the inside. there is a vibration that wasn't there before. the tires are to wide for the car? the are p195/60r14's tire size recomnded is p195/70r14's. i just changed the dog bone bushings, maybe the bottom moter mount needs replaced. the car does pull to the left but not hard.it's a 86 2m4 if that helps<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||86SE||07-23-2000||04:10 PM||||My guess is that your allignment is off.  When you drive in a straight line is your steering wheel turned a little to the right?  I dont think its the tires, I have 215 R14 on my rims.  If its not the allignment I would guess its the bearings.  Can you grab the rear tires and move them in and out more that 1/4 of an inch? <P>------------------<BR>'86 Special Edition,<BR>High-Output V-6 Fiero||||reg||1
