Z||000005||batboy||07-23-2000||04:35 PM||||Bad struts or poor alignment can both cause unusual rear tire wear (althought bad struts often cause cupping wear). Other things to consider are worn wheel bearings and worn CV joints. The tire size should not be the problem, lots of folks have bigger tires.<p>[This message has been edited by batboy (edited 07-23-2000).]||||reg||1
